# Target pose in base_link. Only position + the pitch component (about
# target_pose's own local Y axis) are actually driven to zero -- roll/yaw
# are read only to report residual against, never enforced. See
# PositionPitchIkSolver / docs/position_pitch_ik.md.
geometry_msgs/Pose target_pose

# Seed joint configuration for the iterative solve, in the order
# ForwardKinematicsSolver::GetActuatedJointNames() reports (joint_1..joint_5).
# Empty: use the latest /joint_states_in as the seed (falls back to
# all-zero with a logged warning if none has been received yet) -- same
# convention as SolveIk.srv.
float64[] seed_joint_positions
---
# true iff position+pitch converged -- roll/yaw are never part of this,
# regardless of whether a null-space secondary task is configured (see
# ~nullspace_gain).
bool converged
float64[] joint_positions
# [position(m) x,y,z ; orientation(rad, axis-angle) x,y,z] at the returned
# joint_positions -- same layout as SolveIk.srv's residual. Only the
# position and pitch-axis-projected component of the orientation part are
# actually minimized; the rest is informational (whatever roll/yaw the
# solve, and any configured secondary task, happened to settle at).
float64[] residual
int32 iterations
int32 restarts_used
